export const SIGNAL_DEFINITIONS_MD = "# Signal Definitions\n\n35 boolean factors evaluated uniformly across all KPI cohorts. Source: `pipeline/signal_definitions.py` from the market-fit project.\n\nAll factors are boolean (True/False/null). The categorical `art_style` factor is excluded from discrimination analysis and signal alignment.\n\n---\n\n## Merged Signals (overlapping retention/MAU/revenue)\n\n| Signal | Definition |\n|--------|------------|\n| `short_session` | Primary session under 10 min; >20 min = absent |\n| `timer_gating` | Real-time timers (build, chest, stamina, energy) gating progression or return |\n| `collection_drive` | Completionism as motivation driver (collecting characters, items, sets) |\n| `competitive_ranked` | Visible rank / ladder that rises and falls with play |\n| `limited_time_events` | Time-limited events, seasonal content, exclusive rewards, FOMO offers |\n| `variable_reward_loop` | Variable-ratio reinforcement: gacha pulls, random loot, randomized rewards |\n\n## Related Pairs (distinct definitions)\n\n| Signal | Definition |\n|--------|------------|\n| `social_obligation` | Scheduled clan/guild events with participation expectations |\n| `social_spending` | \"Must spend to keep up\" -- alliance arms races, clan warfare spending pressure |\n| `strong_ip` | Pre-existing IP or brand recognition (licensed franchise, celebrity tie-in) |\n| `mass_market_genre_ip` | Genre or theme with universal mainstream recognition (sports, chess, etc.) |\n| `one_touch_input` | Primary interaction is tap/swipe; no virtual joystick or complex controls |\n| `accessible_mechanic` | Core mechanic learnable in under 30 seconds |\n| `universal_player_fantasy` | Core fantasy is broadly appealing / universally understood |\n| `fantasy_aligned` | Core fantasy reinforces the spending loop (monetization fit) |\n\n## Retention-Origin Signals\n\n| Signal | Definition |\n|--------|------------|\n| `multiple_return_triggers` | At least 2 distinct return mechanisms (daily rewards, events, timers, etc.) |\n| `measurable_progression` | Visible, quantifiable progress (rank, collection %, building level, streak count) |\n| `daily_content` | Reward or content gated to daily cadence (daily quests, puzzles, missions) |\n| `streak_mechanic` | Explicit consecutive-day streak counter with rewards |\n\n## MAU-Origin Signals\n\n| Signal | Definition |\n|--------|------------|\n| `free_to_play` | Free to download and play (standard mobile model) |\n| `game_age_gte_2yr` | Game has been live for 2+ years |\n| `non_us_geographic_majority` | More than 50% of MAU is outside the US |\n| `low_arpu` | Revenue per user < $5/year |\n| `content_refresh_cadence` | Regular content updates (live events, seasons, new levels) |\n| `ad_supported_monetization` | Meaningful ad revenue stream (rewarded video, interstitials) |\n| `social_multiplayer` | Core loop involves playing with/against other people |\n| `regional_cultural_fit` | Game has strong cultural resonance in specific regions |\n| `games_as_social_infra` | Game serves as a social platform beyond gameplay (hangout, chat) |\n| `network_effects_local_play` | Game benefits from local/same-device multiplayer or friend networks |\n| `ugc_platform_model` | User-generated content is a core part of the experience |\n\n## Revenue-Origin Signals\n\n| Signal | Definition |\n|--------|------------|\n| `iap_primary` | IAP is the primary revenue model (not ad-only, subscription-only, or BP-only) |\n| `escalating_spending` | Purchase motivation increases with progression (power creep, harder levels) |\n| `failure_trigger` | Failure/frustration triggers purchase offers (boosters, extra moves, energy) |\n| `pvp_battlepass` | Competitive PvP combined with seasonal battle pass and IAP |\n| `meta_narrative` | Decoration, story, or narrative layer beyond the core loop |\n\n## New Signals\n\n| Signal | Definition |\n|--------|------------|\n| `portrait_orientation` | Primary screen orientation is portrait or both; false = landscape-only |\n";

export const ARCHETYPE_REFERENCE_MD = "# Archetype Reference\n\nAll data from the market-fit project's build artifacts and reports. This file provides the strategic analysis framework for the archetype alignment skill.\n\n---\n\n## Classification Rules\n\nFrom `pipeline/signals/_discriminant_analysis.py`. Three-tier prevalence comparison (exemplar vs near-miss vs mid-range). First matching rule wins:\n\n| Label | Condition | Meaning |\n|-------|-----------|---------|\n| ELITE_ONLY | exemplar >= 60% AND near-miss < 30% AND mid-range < 15% | High in exemplars, absent in lower tiers |\n| INVERSE | mid-range > exemplar + 10pp | More prevalent in lower tiers |\n| UNIVERSAL | spread (max - min across 3 tiers) <= 15pp | Similar prevalence across all tiers |\n| GRADIENT (smooth) | exemplar >= near-miss >= mid-range AND (exemplar - mid-range) > 20pp | Prevalence declines smoothly top to bottom |\n| GRADIENT (partial) | exemplar > near-miss AND (exemplar - mid-range) > 15pp | Prevalence declines from top to bottom |\n| WEAK_GRADIENT | exemplar > mid-range | Small decline from top to bottom |\n| AMBIGUOUS | (else) | No clear pattern |\n\nEffect size is Cramer's V on the 2x2 table (exemplar present/absent vs pooled counter present/absent).\n\nStatistical confidence uses Benjamini-Hochberg FDR: `high` if adjusted p < 0.05, `low` otherwise.\n\n---\n\n## Discrimination Classifications\n\nThese tables provide the per-signal, per-KPI data needed to explain why recipes and archetypes work.\n\n### Retention (D30 >= 20%, n=24 exemplars, n=58 near-miss, n=52 mid-range)\n\n| Signal | Classification | Exemplar % | Mid-range % | Effect Size | Confidence |\n|--------|---------------|----------:|----------:|----------:|-----------|\n| short_session | UNIVERSAL | 8.3 | 7.7 | 0.010 | low |\n| timer_gating | UNIVERSAL | 0.0 | 5.8 | 0.125 | low |\n| collection_drive | UNIVERSAL | 66.7 | 69.2 | 0.031 | low |\n| competitive_ranked | INVERSE | 54.2 | 65.4 | 0.046 | low |\n| limited_time_events | UNIVERSAL | 66.7 | 75.0 | 0.028 | low |\n| variable_reward_loop | UNIVERSAL | 66.7 | 73.1 | 0.003 | low |\n| social_obligation | UNIVERSAL | 62.5 | 69.2 | 0.002 | low |\n| social_spending | UNIVERSAL | 50.0 | 59.6 | 0.014 | low |\n| strong_ip | GRADIENT | 50.0 | 28.8 | 0.179 | low |\n| mass_market_genre_ip | UNIVERSAL | 29.2 | 30.8 | 0.015 | low |\n| one_touch_input | UNIVERSAL | 62.5 | 71.2 | 0.054 | low |\n| accessible_mechanic | UNIVERSAL | 54.2 | 59.6 | 0.053 | low |\n| universal_player_fantasy | UNIVERSAL | 75.0 | 61.5 | 0.071 | low |\n| fantasy_aligned | GRADIENT | 95.8 | 65.4 | 0.279 | high |\n| multiple_return_triggers | UNIVERSAL | 66.7 | 73.1 | 0.012 | low |\n| measurable_progression | UNIVERSAL | 70.8 | 75.0 | 0.007 | low |\n| daily_content | INVERSE | 62.5 | 73.1 | 0.024 | low |\n| streak_mechanic | UNIVERSAL | 37.5 | 32.7 | 0.070 | low |\n| free_to_play | UNIVERSAL | 100.0 | 100.0 | -- | low |\n| game_age_gte_2yr | UNIVERSAL | 100.0 | 100.0 | -- | low |\n| non_us_geographic_majority | UNIVERSAL | 45.8 | 38.5 | 0.046 | low |\n| low_arpu | GRADIENT | 45.8 | 21.2 | 0.121 | low |\n| content_refresh_cadence | UNIVERSAL | 66.7 | 75.0 | 0.020 | low |\n| ad_supported_monetization | UNIVERSAL | 4.2 | 3.8 | 0.032 | low |\n| social_multiplayer | INVERSE | 62.5 | 73.1 | 0.039 | low |\n| regional_cultural_fit | WEAK_GRADIENT | 70.8 | 59.6 | 0.174 | low |\n| games_as_social_infra | UNIVERSAL | 20.8 | 7.7 | 0.128 | low |\n| network_effects_local_play | UNIVERSAL | 62.5 | 69.2 | 0.009 | low |\n| ugc_platform_model | UNIVERSAL | 8.3 | 5.8 | 0.065 | low |\n| iap_primary | INVERSE | 62.5 | 73.1 | 0.031 | low |\n| escalating_spending | INVERSE | 58.3 | 69.2 | 0.042 | low |\n| failure_trigger | INVERSE | 58.3 | 69.2 | 0.057 | low |\n| pvp_battlepass | INVERSE | 45.8 | 65.4 | 0.088 | low |\n| meta_narrative | INVERSE | 50.0 | 65.4 | 0.063 | low |\n| portrait_orientation | GRADIENT | 25.0 | 7.7 | 0.173 | low |\n\n### MAU (> 25M, n=42 exemplars, n=58 near-miss, n=52 mid-range)\n\n| Signal | Classification | Exemplar % | Mid-range % | Effect Size | Confidence |\n|--------|---------------|----------:|----------:|----------:|-----------|\n| short_session | GRADIENT | 23.8 | 7.7 | 0.195 | low |\n| timer_gating | UNIVERSAL | 14.3 | 5.8 | 0.092 | low |\n| collection_drive | UNIVERSAL | 59.5 | 69.2 | 0.030 | low |\n| competitive_ranked | UNIVERSAL | 57.1 | 65.4 | 0.026 | low |\n| limited_time_events | UNIVERSAL | 66.7 | 75.0 | 0.032 | low |\n| variable_reward_loop | UNIVERSAL | 64.3 | 73.1 | 0.020 | low |\n| social_obligation | INVERSE | 57.1 | 69.2 | 0.051 | low |\n| social_spending | INVERSE | 47.6 | 59.6 | 0.038 | low |\n| strong_ip | INVERSE | 16.7 | 28.8 | 0.119 | low |\n| mass_market_genre_ip | GRADIENT | 50.0 | 30.8 | 0.178 | low |\n| one_touch_input | UNIVERSAL | 64.3 | 71.2 | 0.046 | low |\n| accessible_mechanic | UNIVERSAL | 71.4 | 59.6 | 0.098 | low |\n| universal_player_fantasy | GRADIENT | 97.6 | 61.5 | 0.323 | high |\n| fantasy_aligned | UNIVERSAL | 59.5 | 65.4 | 0.021 | low |\n| multiple_return_triggers | UNIVERSAL | 66.7 | 73.1 | 0.015 | low |\n| measurable_progression | UNIVERSAL | 73.8 | 75.0 | 0.038 | low |\n| daily_content | INVERSE | 59.5 | 73.1 | 0.055 | low |\n| streak_mechanic | INVERSE | 7.1 | 32.7 | 0.233 | low |\n| free_to_play | UNIVERSAL | 100.0 | 100.0 | -- | low |\n| game_age_gte_2yr | UNIVERSAL | 100.0 | 100.0 | -- | low |\n| non_us_geographic_majority | GRADIENT | 97.6 | 38.5 | 0.519 | high |\n| low_arpu | GRADIENT | 85.7 | 21.2 | 0.492 | high |\n| content_refresh_cadence | INVERSE | 61.9 | 75.0 | 0.068 | low |\n| ad_supported_monetization | UNIVERSAL | 7.1 | 3.8 | 0.101 | low |\n| social_multiplayer | UNIVERSAL | 64.3 | 73.1 | 0.028 | low |\n| regional_cultural_fit | INVERSE | 9.5 | 59.6 | 0.357 | high |\n| games_as_social_infra | UNIVERSAL | 16.7 | 7.7 | 0.092 | low |\n| network_effects_local_play | UNIVERSAL | 61.9 | 69.2 | 0.016 | low |\n| ugc_platform_model | UNIVERSAL | 7.1 | 5.8 | 0.052 | low |\n| iap_primary | UNIVERSAL | 64.3 | 73.1 | 0.020 | low |\n| escalating_spending | INVERSE | 52.4 | 69.2 | 0.103 | low |\n| failure_trigger | UNIVERSAL | 59.5 | 69.2 | 0.055 | low |\n| pvp_battlepass | INVERSE | 54.8 | 65.4 | 0.023 | low |\n| meta_narrative | INVERSE | 50.0 | 65.4 | 0.074 | low |\n| portrait_orientation | GRADIENT | 23.8 | 7.7 | 0.179 | low |\n\n### Revenue (> $250M/yr, n=33 exemplars, n=58 near-miss, n=52 mid-range)\n\n| Signal | Classification | Exemplar % | Mid-range % | Effect Size | Confidence |\n|--------|---------------|----------:|----------:|----------:|-----------|\n| short_session | UNIVERSAL | 15.2 | 7.7 | 0.083 | low |\n| timer_gating | GRADIENT | 21.2 | 5.8 | 0.174 | low |\n| collection_drive | WEAK_GRADIENT | 78.8 | 69.2 | 0.143 | low |\n| competitive_ranked | GRADIENT | 81.8 | 65.4 | 0.193 | low |\n| limited_time_events | WEAK_GRADIENT | 87.9 | 75.0 | 0.172 | low |\n| variable_reward_loop | WEAK_GRADIENT | 87.9 | 73.1 | 0.200 | low |\n| social_obligation | WEAK_GRADIENT | 81.8 | 69.2 | 0.171 | low |\n| social_spending | WEAK_GRADIENT | 60.6 | 59.6 | 0.074 | low |\n| strong_ip | UNIVERSAL | 39.4 | 28.8 | 0.102 | low |\n| mass_market_genre_ip | UNIVERSAL | 27.3 | 30.8 | 0.033 | low |\n| one_touch_input | UNIVERSAL | 63.6 | 71.2 | 0.049 | low |\n| accessible_mechanic | INVERSE | 48.5 | 59.6 | 0.106 | low |\n| universal_player_fantasy | GRADIENT | 84.8 | 61.5 | 0.171 | low |\n| fantasy_aligned | GRADIENT | 90.9 | 65.4 | 0.264 | high |\n| multiple_return_triggers | WEAK_GRADIENT | 87.9 | 73.1 | 0.186 | low |\n| measurable_progression | WEAK_GRADIENT | 87.9 | 75.0 | 0.172 | low |\n| daily_content | WEAK_GRADIENT | 81.8 | 73.1 | 0.149 | low |\n| streak_mechanic | INVERSE | 21.2 | 32.7 | 0.075 | low |\n| free_to_play | UNIVERSAL | 100.0 | 100.0 | -- | low |\n| game_age_gte_2yr | UNIVERSAL | 100.0 | 100.0 | -- | low |\n| non_us_geographic_majority | GRADIENT | 81.8 | 38.5 | 0.352 | high |\n| low_arpu | INVERSE | 9.1 | 21.2 | 0.210 | low |\n| content_refresh_cadence | WEAK_GRADIENT | 87.9 | 75.0 | 0.179 | low |\n| ad_supported_monetization | UNIVERSAL | 0.0 | 3.8 | 0.080 | low |\n| social_multiplayer | WEAK_GRADIENT | 81.8 | 73.1 | 0.135 | low |\n| regional_cultural_fit | INVERSE | 18.2 | 59.6 | 0.257 | high |\n| games_as_social_infra | UNIVERSAL | 18.2 | 7.7 | 0.107 | low |\n| network_effects_local_play | GRADIENT | 84.8 | 69.2 | 0.193 | low |\n| ugc_platform_model | UNIVERSAL | 6.1 | 5.8 | 0.030 | low |\n| iap_primary | WEAK_GRADIENT | 87.9 | 73.1 | 0.200 | low |\n| escalating_spending | UNIVERSAL | 69.7 | 69.2 | 0.054 | low |\n| failure_trigger | UNIVERSAL | 72.7 | 69.2 | 0.065 | low |\n| pvp_battlepass | AMBIGUOUS | 63.6 | 65.4 | 0.055 | low |\n| meta_narrative | UNIVERSAL | 60.6 | 65.4 | 0.021 | low |\n| portrait_orientation | GRADIENT | 30.3 | 7.7 | 0.242 | low |\n\n---\n\n## Signal Recipes\n\n8 recipes from the market-fit project defining target KPI strategies with signal constraints.\n\n### R-01: Retention-First, Low-ARPU Global Fantasy\n\n**Target KPI:** Retention (D30 >= 20%)\n\n| Category | Signals |\n|----------|---------|\n| MUST HAVE | fantasy_aligned, low_arpu |\n| SAFE BET | universal_player_fantasy, portrait_orientation |\n| TENSION | low_arpu (GRADIENT for Retention and MAU; INVERSE for Revenue) |\n| AVOID | competitive_ranked, daily_content, social_multiplayer, iap_primary, escalating_spending, failure_trigger, pvp_battlepass, meta_narrative |\n\n### R-02: MAU Scale via Short Sessions and Universal Appeal\n\n**Target KPI:** MAU (> 25M)\n\n| Category | Signals |\n|----------|---------|\n| MUST HAVE | universal_player_fantasy, non_us_geographic_majority, low_arpu |\n| SAFE BET | short_session, portrait_orientation |\n| TENSION | low_arpu (GRADIENT for MAU; INVERSE for Revenue) |\n| AVOID | social_obligation, strong_ip, daily_content, streak_mechanic, regional_cultural_fit, meta_narrative |\n\n### R-03: Revenue via Competitive Depth and Global Reach\n\n**Target KPI:** Revenue (> $250M/yr)\n\n| Category | Signals |\n|----------|---------|\n| MUST HAVE | fantasy_aligned, non_us_geographic_majority, competitive_ranked |\n| SAFE BET | universal_player_fantasy, network_effects_local_play, portrait_orientation |\n| TENSION | competitive_ranked (GRADIENT for Revenue; INVERSE for Retention) |\n| AVOID | accessible_mechanic, streak_mechanic, low_arpu, regional_cultural_fit |\n\n### R-04: Triple-KPI via Portrait Accessibility and Universal Fantasy\n\n**Target KPI:** Retention + MAU + Revenue (balanced)\n\n| Category | Signals |\n|----------|---------|\n| MUST HAVE | universal_player_fantasy, fantasy_aligned, portrait_orientation |\n| SAFE BET | non_us_geographic_majority |\n| TENSION | low_arpu vs revenue (supports Retention/MAU but INVERSE for Revenue) |\n| AVOID | streak_mechanic, regional_cultural_fit, daily_content, meta_narrative, pvp_battlepass, escalating_spending |\n\n### R-05: Retention via Strong IP and Fantasy Alignment\n\n**Target KPI:** Retention (D30 >= 20%)\n\n| Category | Signals |\n|----------|---------|\n| MUST HAVE | fantasy_aligned, strong_ip |\n| SAFE BET | portrait_orientation, low_arpu |\n| TENSION | strong_ip (GRADIENT for Retention; INVERSE for MAU) |\n| AVOID | competitive_ranked, daily_content, social_multiplayer, iap_primary, escalating_spending, failure_trigger, pvp_battlepass, meta_narrative |\n\n### R-06: MAU via Mass-Market Genre IP and Non-US Majority\n\n**Target KPI:** MAU (> 25M)\n\n| Category | Signals |\n|----------|---------|\n| MUST HAVE | universal_player_fantasy, non_us_geographic_majority, mass_market_genre_ip |\n| SAFE BET | short_session, low_arpu, portrait_orientation |\n| TENSION | mass_market_genre_ip (MAU GRADIENT; UNIVERSAL for Retention/Revenue) |\n| AVOID | strong_ip, streak_mechanic, regional_cultural_fit, social_obligation, daily_content, meta_narrative |\n\n### R-07: Revenue via Timer Gating and Network Effects (Moonshot)\n\n**Target KPI:** Revenue (> $250M/yr)\n\n| Category | Signals |\n|----------|---------|\n| MUST HAVE | fantasy_aligned, universal_player_fantasy, network_effects_local_play |\n| SAFE BET | non_us_geographic_majority, competitive_ranked, portrait_orientation |\n| TENSION | timer_gating (GRADIENT for Revenue; often conflated with failure_trigger which is Retention INVERSE) |\n| AVOID | accessible_mechanic, streak_mechanic, low_arpu, regional_cultural_fit |\n\n### R-08: MAU + Retention Without Low ARPU (Moonshot)\n\n**Target KPI:** MAU + Retention + Revenue (without low-ARPU trade-off)\n\n| Category | Signals |\n|----------|---------|\n| MUST HAVE | universal_player_fantasy, fantasy_aligned, non_us_geographic_majority |\n| SAFE BET | portrait_orientation, short_session |\n| TENSION | low_arpu (typically GRADIENT for MAU/Retention; this recipe AVOIDs it to pursue revenue -- structural barrier: 85.7% of MAU exemplars have low_arpu) |\n| AVOID | low_arpu, streak_mechanic, regional_cultural_fit, social_obligation, daily_content, meta_narrative |\n\n---\n\n## Mechanical Archetypes\n\n4 archetypes derived from co-occurring GRADIENT signals across KPI cohorts.\n\n### 1. Global Mass-Market Fantasy\n\n**Signals:** universal_player_fantasy, non_us_geographic_majority, fantasy_aligned, low_arpu (optional)\n\n| KPI | Predicted? | Key GRADIENT signals |\n|-----|-----------|---------------------|\n| Retention | Yes | fantasy_aligned, low_arpu |\n| MAU | Yes | universal_player_fantasy, non_us_geographic_majority, low_arpu |\n| Revenue | Partial | universal_player_fantasy, fantasy_aligned, non_us_geographic_majority |\n\n**Tension:** low_arpu supports reach and retention but INVERSE for revenue. Revenue exemplars offset with competitive_ranked, network_effects_local_play, or premium IP.\n\n**Evidence:** Clash Royale, Free Fire, Brawl Stars (triple-KPI), Mobile Legends, PUBG MOBILE.\n\n### 2. Competitive PvP with Social Depth\n\n**Signals:** competitive_ranked, network_effects_local_play, fantasy_aligned, universal_player_fantasy\n\n| KPI | Predicted? | Key GRADIENT signals |\n|-----|-----------|---------------------|\n| Retention | Yes | fantasy_aligned |\n| MAU | Yes | universal_player_fantasy |\n| Revenue | Yes | competitive_ranked, network_effects_local_play, universal_player_fantasy, fantasy_aligned |\n\n**Tension:** competitive and social mechanics drive revenue and retention but can increase complexity and reduce accessibility for MAU scale.\n\n**Evidence:** Clash Royale, Brawl Stars, PUBG MOBILE, eFootball.\n\n### 3. Portrait-Oriented, Accessible Core Loop\n\n**Signals:** portrait_orientation, universal_player_fantasy, accessible_mechanic (UNIVERSAL but prevalent)\n\n| KPI | Predicted? | Key GRADIENT signals |\n|-----|-----------|---------------------|\n| Retention | Yes | portrait_orientation |\n| MAU | Yes | portrait_orientation, universal_player_fantasy |\n| Revenue | Yes | portrait_orientation, universal_player_fantasy |\n\n**Tension:** portrait orientation and accessibility support all KPIs but may limit genre scope.\n\n**Evidence:** Avatar World, Royal Match, Candy Crush Saga.\n\n### 4. Short-Session MAU Scale\n\n**Signals:** short_session, universal_player_fantasy, non_us_geographic_majority, low_arpu\n\n| KPI | Predicted? | Key GRADIENT signals |\n|-----|-----------|---------------------|\n| Retention | No | short_session is UNIVERSAL for retention |\n| MAU | Yes | short_session, universal_player_fantasy, non_us_geographic_majority, low_arpu |\n| Revenue | No | low_arpu is INVERSE for revenue |\n\n**Tension:** optimized for MAU scale via short sessions and low ARPU; typically weak on retention and revenue.\n\n**Evidence:** Block Blast!, Subway Surfers.\n\n---\n\n## ARPU Segmentation Divergences\n\nRevenue exemplars split at $20/yr ARPU: high-ARPU (n=24) vs volume (n=9).\n\n### Convergence Signals (same classification in both sub-cohorts)\n\n| Signal | Classification | High-ARPU % | Volume % |\n|--------|---------------|----------:|--------:|\n| fantasy_aligned | GRADIENT | 91.7 | 88.9 |\n| universal_player_fantasy | GRADIENT | 79.2 | 100.0 |\n| non_us_geographic_majority | GRADIENT | 75.0 | 100.0 |\n| portrait_orientation | GRADIENT | 25.0 | 44.4 |\n| regional_cultural_fit | INVERSE | 20.8 | 11.1 |\n\n### Divergence Signals (different classification by sub-cohort)\n\n| Signal | High-ARPU | Volume | High-ARPU % | Volume % |\n|--------|-----------|--------|----------:|--------:|\n| meta_narrative | WEAK_GRADIENT | INVERSE | 75.0 | 22.2 |\n| pvp_battlepass | INVERSE | GRADIENT | 54.2 | 88.9 |\n| low_arpu | INVERSE | WEAK_GRADIENT | 0.0 | 33.3 |\n| one_touch_input | UNIVERSAL | INVERSE | 70.8 | 44.4 |\n| competitive_ranked | WEAK_GRADIENT | GRADIENT | 75.0 | 100.0 |\n| social_obligation | WEAK_GRADIENT | GRADIENT | 75.0 | 100.0 |\n| social_multiplayer | UNIVERSAL | GRADIENT | 75.0 | 100.0 |\n| social_spending | UNIVERSAL | GRADIENT | 54.2 | 77.8 |\n| ugc_platform_model | UNIVERSAL | GRADIENT | 0.0 | 22.2 |\n| games_as_social_infra | UNIVERSAL | GRADIENT | 12.5 | 33.3 |\n| network_effects_local_play | WEAK_GRADIENT | GRADIENT | 79.2 | 100.0 |\n| streak_mechanic | UNIVERSAL | INVERSE | 25.0 | 11.1 |\n| accessible_mechanic | UNIVERSAL | INVERSE | 50.0 | 44.4 |\n| timer_gating | UNIVERSAL | GRADIENT | 20.8 | 22.2 |\n\n---\n\n## Cross-KPI Tension Patterns\n\nSignals that predict one KPI but conflict with another.\n\n| Signal | Predicts | Conflicts With | Trade-off |\n|--------|----------|---------------|-----------|\n| low_arpu | MAU (GRADIENT, 85.7% vs 21.2%), Retention (GRADIENT, 45.8% vs 21.2%) | Revenue (INVERSE, 9.1% vs 21.2%) | MAU scale via low monetization; Revenue requires higher ARPU |\n| competitive_ranked | Revenue (GRADIENT, 81.8% vs 65.4%) | Retention (INVERSE, 54.2% vs 65.4%) | Ranked PvP drives revenue but rank anxiety can hurt retention |\n| strong_ip | Retention (GRADIENT, 50.0% vs 28.8%) | MAU (INVERSE, 16.7% vs 28.8%) | IP lifts retention via fandom but limits MAU reach |\n| regional_cultural_fit | -- | MAU (INVERSE, 9.5% vs 59.6%), Revenue (INVERSE, 18.2% vs 59.6%) | Region-specific games rarely reach global scale or revenue |\n| short_session | MAU (GRADIENT, 23.8% vs 7.7%) | -- (UNIVERSAL for Retention and Revenue) | MAU favors quick sessions; neutral for other KPIs |\n| portrait_orientation | All 3 KPIs (GRADIENT for all) | -- | Rare signal with no tension; supports all KPIs |\n\n---\n\n## Sentiment Wedge Opportunities\n\n7 wedge opportunities where player pain meets design innovation potential.\n\n| # | Wedge | Opportunity |\n|---|-------|------------|\n| 1 | Transparent matchmaking | Display matchmaking criteria; reduce perception of unfair pairing |\n| 2 | Fair monetization without pressure | Monetize cosmetics/convenience without gating core progression |\n| 3 | F2P-friendly progression | Reduce time-to-viable; deterministic progression; separate power from cosmetics |\n| 4 | Technical reliability | Optimize for low-end devices; reduce desync; improve reconnection |\n| 5 | Content freshness | Procedural or modular content; vary event formats; add new loops |\n| 6 | Social obligation without toxicity | Clan systems that create positive obligation without peer pressure |\n| 7 | Skill-first competitive | Emphasize skill expression; reduce RNG in ranked; transparent power progression |\n";

